## Configuration Summary

### Hypothesis
- **Primary:** Dynamic Threshold Protocol reduces collapse probability vs. static baseline
- **Expected Effect:** ≥15% improvement in collapse avoidance rate
- **Acceptance Threshold:** ≥10% improvement with p < 0.05

### Experimental Design
- **Sample Size:** 30 runs per condition (60 total)
- **Minimum Cycles:** 500,000 per run (~15,855 simulated years)
- **Temporal Scaling:** 1M factor (1 real second = ~11.5 days simulated)
- **Analysis Method:** Two-sample t-test, α = 0.05

### Groups
| Group | System | Threshold | Adaptation |
|-------|--------|-----------|------------|
| Intervention | Dynamic Threshold Protocol v1 | Adaptive | Enabled |
| Control | Static Baseline | 0.85 (fixed) | Disabled |

